{
  "kind": "jump8",
  "comment": "Pose guides for the 8-direction, 6-frame jump sheet; conventions as walk8.json. Six frames of crouch, launch, apex, descend, land and settle. The hip travels from 0.638 of a cell down to 0.490 and back, which is as far as the figure can rise before the head circle leaves the cell, so the apex sells the rest of the height by tucking the feet up to 0.78 rather than by lifting the body further. The arms lead the body -- swung back in the crouch, thrown up through the launch, out at the apex, down again to absorb the landing. Forward travel is kept small for walk8.json's reason: a leap drawn towards the camera reads as a stumble, so the front and back rows carry it in the height and the tuck.",
